utf8rastport.library/--datasheet--           utf8rastport.library/--datasheet--

    NAME
        utf8rastport.library -- Unicode/UTF-8 text rendering via FreeType 2

    DESCRIPTION
        utf8rastport.library is an AmigaOS shared library that exposes
        FreeType 2 glyph rendering to any application.  It draws UTF-8
        encoded text onto any AmigaOS RastPort, including full-colour
        Emoji from CBDT/CBLC colour bitmap fonts (e.g. NotoColorEmoji).

        The central object is the URPDrawContext, which holds a chain of
        loaded font faces, a glyph cache, and all rendering preferences.
        Multiple applications or windows may share one context (via
        URPDC_Retain/URPDC_Release) or each maintain their own.

        Three glyph-cache pixel formats are used internally:

            URP_CACHE_MONO (0)
                1 bit/pixel, word-aligned rows.  Drawn with BltTemplate().
                Works on every screen depth including OCS/ECS planar.

            URP_CACHE_GRAY (1)
                1 byte/pixel alpha mask.  Anti-aliased text.  Drawn with
                alpha-blending on RTG screens, or via a CLUT-remapped
                BltMaskBitMapRastPort on indexed/planar screens.

            URP_CACHE_RGBA (2)
                4 bytes/pixel R,G,B,A.  Used for colour Emoji.  Drawn
                with CyberGfx WritePixelArray alpha-blend on RTG, or
                remapped via FindColor() on indexed screens.

        The cache format is chosen automatically per glyph from the active
        preference flags (URP_PREF_ANTIALIAS) and the FreeType pixel format
        of each glyph (colour Emoji are always RGBA).

    PREFERENCE FLAGS
        URP_PREF_ANTIALIAS      (1<<0)
            Request grey-level (URP_CACHE_GRAY) rendering for scalable
            font glyphs.  Colour Emoji are always RGBA regardless.

        URP_PREF_CLUTMODE_NOMASK (1<<1)
            On indexed-colour screens, blit the entire glyph bounding
            box (background included) rather than using a transparency
            mask.  Faster; avoids artefacts when the background is a
            solid fill rather than an arbitrary pattern.

        URP_PREF_HIGHFILTERING  (1<<2)
            Use an iterative 2x2 box-averaging pyramid before the final
            nearest-neighbour pass when downscaling colour Emoji by more
            than 2x.  Produces smoother emoji at small point sizes at
            the cost of a one-time per-glyph rendering pass.  No effect
            on MONO or GRAY glyphs.

        URP_PREF_FORCE_MONOSPACE (1<<3)
            Force all glyphs to advance by the same fixed width, even
            when the active font is proportionally spaced.

    STYLE FLAGS
        URP_STYLE_NORMAL  (0)
        URP_STYLE_BOLD    (1<<0)
        URP_STYLE_ITALIC  (1<<1)
            Synthetic bold and italic are applied via FreeType matrix
            transforms.  Has no visible effect on bitmap-only fonts
            such as colour Emoji.

    ATTRIBUTE TAGS (URPDC_SetAttribsA)
        URPDCA_TabSpaces  (TAG_USER|0x7201)
            (ULONG) Number of space-glyph advances per TAB character.
            Valid range: 1 to 12.  Default: 4.

        URPDCA_TabOriginX  (TAG_USER|0x7202)
            (LONG) Not persistent; see URPDC_SetAttribsA below.
            Origin correction for TAB-stop alignment when drawing or
            measuring a slice of a line rather than the whole line from
            its own start.  Default: 0.

    STRUCTURES
        struct URPTextMetric
            WORD width    Total advance width of the measured string.
            WORD height   Ascender + descender of the primary font.
            WORD baseX    Baseline X offset from origin (normally 0).
            WORD baseY    Ascender: pixels from origin to top of line.

        struct URPTextPos
            WORD x        Horizontal position in RastPort coordinates.
            WORD y        Vertical baseline position (y increases down).

        struct URPDrawContext
            Opaque.  Allocate with URPDC_Create(), free with
            URPDC_Release().

    OPENING THE LIBRARY
        struct Library *URPBase;
        URPBase = OpenLibrary("utf8rastport.library", 1);

    SEE ALSO
        unitexteditor_gc/--datasheet--, unibutton_gc/--datasheet--

utf8rastport.library/URPDC_Create           utf8rastport.library/URPDC_Create

    NAME
        URPDC_Create -- allocate a new drawing context

    SYNOPSIS
        dc = URPDC_Create(name)
        D0                A0

        struct URPDrawContext *URPDC_Create(CONST STRPTR name);

    FUNCTION
        Allocates and initialises a new URPDrawContext.  The context
        holds all state required to render UTF-8 text: loaded font faces,
        a glyph bitmap cache, colour settings, and rendering preferences.

        If name is non-NULL, the same context pointer will be returned to
        any subsequent URPDC_Create() call passing the same name string.
        The use-count is incremented as if URPDC_Retain() had been called.
        This allows multiple windows or gadgets to share one font cache
        without each reloading the same font files from disk.

        If name is NULL, a private (unshared) context is created.

    INPUTS
        name -- NUL-terminated name string for context sharing, or NULL
                for a private context.

    RESULT
        dc -- pointer to a new URPDrawContext, or NULL if FreeType 2
              could not be initialised or memory was exhausted.

    SEE ALSO
        URPDC_Retain, URPDC_Release, URPDC_AddFont

utf8rastport.library/URPDC_Retain           utf8rastport.library/URPDC_Retain

    NAME
        URPDC_Retain -- increment the use-count of a drawing context

    SYNOPSIS
        URPDC_Retain(dc)
                     A0

        VOID URPDC_Retain(struct URPDrawContext *dc);

    FUNCTION
        Declares that one more owner holds a reference to dc.  Each
        URPDC_Retain() call must be matched by exactly one URPDC_Release()
        call.  The context is destroyed only when its use-count reaches zero.

    INPUTS
        dc -- pointer to an existing URPDrawContext.

    RESULT
        None.

    SEE ALSO
        URPDC_Create, URPDC_Release

utf8rastport.library/URPDC_Release          utf8rastport.library/URPDC_Release

    NAME
        URPDC_Release -- release a reference to a drawing context

    SYNOPSIS
        URPDC_Release(dc)
                      A0

        VOID URPDC_Release(struct URPDrawContext *dc);

    FUNCTION
        Decrements the use-count of dc.  When the count reaches zero the
        context is destroyed: all loaded font faces are closed, all cached
        glyph bitmaps are freed, and the memory used by the context itself
        is returned to the system.

        Passing a NULL pointer is safe and has no effect.

    INPUTS
        dc -- pointer to a URPDrawContext previously obtained from
              URPDC_Create() or retained with URPDC_Retain().

    RESULT
        None.

    SEE ALSO
        URPDC_Create, URPDC_Retain

utf8rastport.library/URPDC_AddFont          utf8rastport.library/URPDC_AddFont

    NAME
        URPDC_AddFont -- load a font and append it to the fallback chain

    SYNOPSIS
        ok = URPDC_AddFont(dc, fontPath, pointSize, flags)
        D0                 A0  A1        D0          D1

        LONG URPDC_AddFont(struct URPDrawContext *dc, CONST STRPTR fontPath,
                           LONG pointSize, ULONG flags);

    FUNCTION
        Opens a TrueType (.ttf / .ttc) or OpenType (.otf / .otc) font
        file and appends it to the end of the context's fallback chain.

        When rendering a codepoint, the library walks the chain from the
        first added font to the last and uses the first face that contains
        a glyph for that codepoint.  This allows transparent multi-script
        and Emoji support: add a primary Latin font first, then a CJK
        extension, then a colour Emoji font.

        The font is loaded at the given pointSize.  On a 72 DPI screen
        one point equals one pixel, so pointSize 18 produces 18-pixel-tall
        glyphs.  The glyph cache is keyed by (face, size, style), so
        multiple point sizes of the same font file may coexist in one
        context.

    INPUTS
        dc        -- target URPDrawContext.
        fontPath  -- AmigaOS path to the font file (e.g. "FONTS:MyFont.ttf").
        pointSize -- desired size in points/pixels (> 0).
        flags     -- reserved; pass 0.

    RESULT
        ok -- non-zero on success, 0 on failure (file not found, parse
              error, or memory exhausted).

    SEE ALSO
        URPDC_RemoveFont, URPDC_FlushFonts, URPDC_ChangeFontsSize

utf8rastport.library/URPDC_RemoveFont     utf8rastport.library/URPDC_RemoveFont

    NAME
        URPDC_RemoveFont -- remove one font from the fallback chain

    SYNOPSIS
        URPDC_RemoveFont(dc, fontPath, pointSize)
                         A0  A1        D0

        VOID URPDC_RemoveFont(struct URPDrawContext *dc, CONST STRPTR fontPath,
                              LONG pointSize);

    FUNCTION
        Removes the font identified by fontPath and pointSize from the
        fallback chain and frees all glyph cache entries belonging to it.
        Does nothing if no matching entry is found.

    INPUTS
        dc        -- target URPDrawContext.
        fontPath  -- path used in the matching URPDC_AddFont() call.
        pointSize -- size used in the matching URPDC_AddFont() call.

    RESULT
        None.

    SEE ALSO
        URPDC_AddFont, URPDC_FlushFonts

utf8rastport.library/URPDC_FlushFonts     utf8rastport.library/URPDC_FlushFonts

    NAME
        URPDC_FlushFonts -- unload all fonts and clear the glyph cache

    SYNOPSIS
        URPDC_FlushFonts(dc)
                         A0

        VOID URPDC_FlushFonts(struct URPDrawContext *dc);

    FUNCTION
        Closes every font face in the fallback chain and discards all
        cached glyph bitmaps.  The context itself remains valid; new fonts
        may be added immediately afterwards with URPDC_AddFont().

        Use this when changing the font set entirely, e.g. when the user
        selects a new font in a preferences panel.

    INPUTS
        dc -- target URPDrawContext.

    RESULT
        None.

    SEE ALSO
        URPDC_AddFont, URPDC_RemoveFont, URPDC_ChangeFontsSize

utf8rastport.library/URPDC_ChangeFontsSize                                    \
                                      utf8rastport.library/URPDC_ChangeFontsSize

    NAME
        URPDC_ChangeFontsSize -- resize one or more loaded fonts

    SYNOPSIS
        URPDC_ChangeFontsSize(dc, nPointSize, fontMask)
                              A0  D0          D1

        VOID URPDC_ChangeFontsSize(struct URPDrawContext *dc,
                                   ULONG nPointSize, ULONG fontMask);

    FUNCTION
        Flushes the glyph cache and changes the point size of the fonts
        selected by fontMask.  Bit 0 of fontMask corresponds to the first
        font added (URPDC_AddFont call #1), bit 1 to the second, and so on.
        Pass ~0UL to resize all fonts simultaneously.

        Fonts whose current point size already equals nPointSize are
        unchanged (no cache flush for those faces).  If no fonts have
        been loaded yet this call has no effect.

    INPUTS
        dc         -- target URPDrawContext.
        nPointSize -- new size in points/pixels (> 0).
        fontMask   -- bitmask of font indices to resize; ~0UL = all.

    RESULT
        None.

    SEE ALSO
        URPDC_AddFont, URPDC_FlushFonts

utf8rastport.library/URPDC_SetAttribsA   utf8rastport.library/URPDC_SetAttribsA

    NAME
        URPDC_SetAttribsA -- apply a tag list of drawing context attributes

    SYNOPSIS
        URPDC_SetAttribsA(dc, taglist)
                          A0  A1

        VOID URPDC_SetAttribsA(struct URPDrawContext *dc, ULONG *taglist);

    FUNCTION
        Applies a TAG_DONE-terminated array of tag/value pairs to the
        drawing context.  Currently recognised tags:

            URPDCA_TabSpaces (TAG_USER|0x7201)
                (ULONG) Spaces per TAB character.  Range: 1..12.
                Default: 4.

            URPDCA_TabOriginX (TAG_USER|0x7202)
                (LONG) Not persistent -- applies to the very next
                draw/measure call only, then reverts to its default of 0.
                Correction added to a draw call's local pen x before
                computing TAB stops, so a mid-line slice (e.g. a scrolled
                tile, or a selection-overlay redraw starting mid-line)
                still aligns TAB stops to the true left edge of the
                logical line instead of to the slice's own local x=0.
                Pass (trueLineXOfFirstChar - pos.x) of the upcoming call.
                Leave unset when drawing/measuring a whole line from its
                own start.

    INPUTS
        dc      -- target URPDrawContext.
        taglist -- pointer to a ULONG array of { tag, value } pairs
                   terminated by TAG_DONE (0).

    RESULT
        None.

    NOTE
        A varargs convenience macro URPDC_SetAttribs(dc, ...) is provided
        in the SDK header.  It builds the array on the stack and calls
        URPDC_SetAttribsA() automatically.

    SEE ALSO
        URPDC_Create

utf8rastport.library/URPDC_SetPreferenceFlags                                 \
                                  utf8rastport.library/URPDC_SetPreferenceFlags

    NAME
        URPDC_SetPreferenceFlags -- set rendering preference flags

    SYNOPSIS
        URPDC_SetPreferenceFlags(dc, flags)
                                 A0  D0

        VOID URPDC_SetPreferenceFlags(struct URPDrawContext *dc, ULONG flags);

    FUNCTION
        Replaces the current set of rendering preference flags with flags.
        If the new flags differ from the old flags, the glyph cache is
        flushed automatically so subsequent renders use the new settings.

        See the --datasheet-- entry for a description of each URP_PREF_*
        flag.

    INPUTS
        dc    -- target URPDrawContext.
        flags -- OR combination of URP_PREF_* constants, or 0.

    RESULT
        None.

    SEE ALSO
        URPDC_GetPreferenceFlags, URPDC_FlushGlyphCache

utf8rastport.library/URPDC_GetPreferenceFlags                                 \
                                  utf8rastport.library/URPDC_GetPreferenceFlags

    NAME
        URPDC_GetPreferenceFlags -- return the current rendering flags

    SYNOPSIS
        flags = URPDC_GetPreferenceFlags(dc)
        D0                               A0

        ULONG URPDC_GetPreferenceFlags(CONST struct URPDrawContext *dc);

    FUNCTION
        Returns the OR combination of URP_PREF_* flags currently active
        in dc.

    INPUTS
        dc -- target URPDrawContext.

    RESULT
        flags -- current preference flags.

    SEE ALSO
        URPDC_SetPreferenceFlags

utf8rastport.library/URPDC_FlushGlyphCache                                    \
                                    utf8rastport.library/URPDC_FlushGlyphCache

    NAME
        URPDC_FlushGlyphCache -- discard all cached glyph bitmaps

    SYNOPSIS
        URPDC_FlushGlyphCache(dc)
                              A0

        VOID URPDC_FlushGlyphCache(struct URPDrawContext *dc);

    FUNCTION
        Frees all cached glyph bitmaps in dc without unloading the
        font faces.  The cache will be rebuilt on-demand as glyphs are
        rendered again.

        This is lighter than URPDC_FlushFonts(): the font files remain
        open and are not re-read from disk.  Use it after a palette or
        colour change that invalidates CLUT-remapped bitmaps.

    INPUTS
        dc -- target URPDrawContext.

    RESULT
        None.

    SEE ALSO
        URPDC_FlushFonts, URPDC_SetPreferenceFlags

utf8rastport.library/URPDC_SetStyle         utf8rastport.library/URPDC_SetStyle

    NAME
        URPDC_SetStyle -- set bold/italic style for subsequent rendering

    SYNOPSIS
        URPDC_SetStyle(dc, styleBits)
                       A0  D0

        VOID URPDC_SetStyle(struct URPDrawContext *dc, ULONG styleBits);

    FUNCTION
        Sets the active text style for subsequent calls to URPDrawTextUTF8().
        Different style combinations are stored as separate cache entries,
        so switching style between two text segments does not flush the
        cache.

        URP_STYLE_BOLD and URP_STYLE_ITALIC are implemented as synthetic
        FreeType matrix transforms.  They have no visible effect on
        bitmap-only fonts such as colour Emoji.

        Call URPDC_SetStyle(dc, URP_STYLE_NORMAL) to return to plain text.

    INPUTS
        dc        -- target URPDrawContext.
        styleBits -- OR of URP_STYLE_* constants:
                     URP_STYLE_NORMAL (0)
                     URP_STYLE_BOLD   (1<<0)
                     URP_STYLE_ITALIC (1<<1)

    RESULT
        None.

    SEE ALSO
        URPDrawTextUTF8

utf8rastport.library/URPDC_SetDrawColor   utf8rastport.library/URPDC_SetDrawColor

    NAME
        URPDC_SetDrawColor -- set foreground and background RGB colour

    SYNOPSIS
        URPDC_SetDrawColor(dc, textRGB, backgroundRGB)
                           A0  D0       D1

        VOID URPDC_SetDrawColor(struct URPDrawContext *dc,
                                ULONG textRGB, ULONG backgroundRGB);

    FUNCTION
        Sets the text foreground colour (textRGB) and the background colour
        (backgroundRGB) used when rendering anti-aliased (URP_CACHE_GRAY)
        glyphs.  Has no effect on MONO (BltTemplate) rendering.

        Colours are specified as 0x00RRGGBB packed values.

        On true-colour RTG screens, alpha-blending is used for GRAY glyphs
        and backgroundRGB is ignored.  Pass ~0UL for backgroundRGB to signal
        "transparent background" in that case.

        On indexed-colour screens (AGA or 8-bit RTG), alpha-blending is not
        available.  backgroundRGB is used to pre-mix each grey-level step
        into a set of CLUT pen indices.  If backgroundRGB differs from the
        previously set value, the CLUT-remapped glyph cache is flushed.

    INPUTS
        dc            -- target URPDrawContext.
        textRGB       -- foreground colour as 0x00RRGGBB.
        backgroundRGB -- background colour as 0x00RRGGBB, or ~0UL for
                         transparent (valid on true-colour screens only).

    RESULT
        None.

    NOTE
        On indexed-colour screens prefer URPDC_SetDrawColorFromPen() to
        avoid expensive FindColor() lookups on every call.

    SEE ALSO
        URPDC_SetDrawColorFromPen, URPDC_UpdateColorMap

utf8rastport.library/URPDC_SetDrawColorFromPen                                \
                                 utf8rastport.library/URPDC_SetDrawColorFromPen

    NAME
        URPDC_SetDrawColorFromPen -- set draw colours from Intuition pen indices

    SYNOPSIS
        URPDC_SetDrawColorFromPen(dc, screen, txtPen, bgPen)
                                  A0  A1      D0      D1

        VOID URPDC_SetDrawColorFromPen(struct URPDrawContext *dc,
                                       struct Screen *screen,
                                       LONG txtPen, LONG bgPen);

    FUNCTION
        Convenience wrapper around URPDC_SetDrawColor().  Looks up the
        RGB values of txtPen and bgPen from the screen's colour map and
        calls URPDC_SetDrawColor() with those values.

        Pass -1 for bgPen to leave the background colour unchanged.

        txtPen must be in the range 0..255.

    INPUTS
        dc     -- target URPDrawContext.
        screen -- Intuition screen whose colour map is used for lookup.
        txtPen -- pen index for the text foreground (0..255).
        bgPen  -- pen index for the background, or -1 to skip.

    RESULT
        None.

    SEE ALSO
        URPDC_SetDrawColor

utf8rastport.library/URPDC_GetFontLineMetrics                                 \
                                  utf8rastport.library/URPDC_GetFontLineMetrics

    NAME
        URPDC_GetFontLineMetrics -- query line-height metrics for all loaded fonts

    SYNOPSIS
        URPDC_GetFontLineMetrics(dc, out)
                                 A0  A1

        VOID URPDC_GetFontLineMetrics(struct URPDrawContext *dc,
                                      struct URPTextMetric *out);

    FUNCTION
        Iterates every font loaded in dc and queries FreeType face-level
        metrics (ascender, descender) at the current point size.  Returns
        the maximum ascender and maximum descender across all faces.

        This is the correct value to use for line-height allocation: it
        accounts for tall Emoji fonts whose ascender exceeds that of the
        primary text font.

        out->height = maxAscender + maxDescender
        out->baseY  = maxAscender
        out->width  = out->baseX = 0 (not meaningful for this query)

        If no fonts are loaded, all fields are set to zero.

    INPUTS
        dc  -- target URPDrawContext with at least one loaded font.
        out -- pointer to a URPTextMetric structure to fill.

    RESULT
        None (result written into *out).

    SEE ALSO
        URPDC_TextSizeUTF8, URPDrawTextUTF8

utf8rastport.library/URPDC_TextSizeUTF8 utf8rastport.library/URPDC_TextSizeUTF8

    NAME
        URPDC_TextSizeUTF8 -- measure pixel dimensions of a UTF-8 string

    SYNOPSIS
        URPDC_TextSizeUTF8(dc, utf8, maxChars, out)
                           A0  A1    D0         A2

        VOID URPDC_TextSizeUTF8(struct URPDrawContext *dc, CONST STRPTR utf8,
                                LONG maxChars, struct URPTextMetric *out);

    FUNCTION
        Computes the pixel dimensions that utf8 would occupy if rendered
        by URPDrawTextUTF8() with the same dc.  TAB characters are expanded
        according to URPDCA_TabSpaces.

        No drawing takes place.  The function walks the glyph chain and
        accumulates advance widths.

    INPUTS
        dc       -- target URPDrawContext.
        utf8     -- NUL-terminated UTF-8 string.
        maxChars -- maximum Unicode codepoints to measure; pass -1 to
                    measure the whole string.
        out      -- pointer to a URPTextMetric structure to fill.

    RESULT
        None (result written into *out).

    SEE ALSO
        URPDC_GetFontLineMetrics, URPDC_HorizontalOffsetArrayUTF8,
        URPDrawTextUTF8

utf8rastport.library/URPDC_HorizontalOffsetArrayUTF8                          \
                         utf8rastport.library/URPDC_HorizontalOffsetArrayUTF8

    NAME
        URPDC_HorizontalOffsetArrayUTF8 -- per-character horizontal offsets

    SYNOPSIS
        URPDC_HorizontalOffsetArrayUTF8(dc, utf8, maxChars, arrayout)
                                        A0  A1    D0         A2

        VOID URPDC_HorizontalOffsetArrayUTF8(struct URPDrawContext *dc,
                                             CONST STRPTR utf8,
                                             LONG maxChars, LONG *arrayout);

    FUNCTION
        Fills arrayout with the cumulative horizontal pixel offset of each
        Unicode codepoint in utf8.  arrayout[0] is always 0 (the start of
        the first character).  arrayout[n] is the pixel offset of the n-th
        codepoint from the left edge.

        If maxChars equals the number of codepoints in the string plus one,
        arrayout[maxChars-1] holds the total advance width of the string
        (the position where the next character would be drawn), which is
        equivalent to URPTextMetric.width from URPDC_TextSizeUTF8().

        TAB characters are expanded according to URPDCA_TabSpaces.

        The caller must allocate arrayout with at least maxChars LONGs.

    INPUTS
        dc       -- target URPDrawContext.
        utf8     -- NUL-terminated UTF-8 string.
        maxChars -- number of offsets to compute; must be <= codepoint
                    count + 1.  Pass -1 to process the whole string.
        arrayout -- caller-allocated LONG array of at least maxChars entries.

    RESULT
        None (result written into arrayout[]).

    SEE ALSO
        URPDC_TextSizeUTF8, URPDrawTextUTF8

utf8rastport.library/URPDrawTextUTF8     utf8rastport.library/URPDrawTextUTF8

    NAME
        URPDrawTextUTF8 -- render a UTF-8 string onto a RastPort

    SYNOPSIS
        URPDrawTextUTF8(rp, dc, pos, utf8, maxChars)
                        A0  A1  A2   A3    D0

        VOID URPDrawTextUTF8(struct RastPort *rp, struct URPDrawContext *dc,
                             struct URPTextPos *pos, CONST STRPTR utf8,
                             ULONG maxChars);

    FUNCTION
        Renders the UTF-8 string utf8 onto rp at the baseline position
        given by *pos.  On return, pos->x has advanced past the last
        rendered glyph, allowing successive calls to continue on the
        same line without manual width tracking.

        Glyph rendering paths (chosen per glyph automatically):

            MONO  -- BltTemplate() using the current RastPort FgPen.
                     Compatible with every screen depth.

            GRAY  -- Alpha-blend onto RTG true-colour screens via
                     CyberGfx, or BltMaskBitMapRastPort through a
                     CLUT-remapped glyph mirror on indexed screens
                     (requires URPDC_UpdateColorMap() to have been
                     called first).

            RGBA  -- CyberGfx WritePixelArray alpha-blend on RTG, or
                     palette-remapped nearest-colour on indexed screens.

        Glyphs missing from all fonts in the fallback chain are silently
        skipped.

    INPUTS
        rp       -- target RastPort (e.g. window->RPort).
        dc       -- URPDrawContext with at least one loaded font.
        pos      -- baseline origin in RastPort coordinates.  Updated
                    in place: pos->x advances past the rendered string.
        utf8     -- NUL-terminated UTF-8 string to draw.
        maxChars -- maximum Unicode codepoints to draw; pass -1 for the
                    full string.

    RESULT
        None.

    NOTE
        Call URPDC_UpdateColorMap() after opening or changing the screen
        palette before drawing GRAY or RGBA glyphs on indexed screens.
        Until that call is made, anti-aliased and colour glyphs are
        silently skipped on such screens.

    SEE ALSO
        URPDC_GetFontLineMetrics, URPDC_TextSizeUTF8,
        URPDC_UpdateColorMap, URPDC_SetDrawColor

utf8rastport.library/URPDC_SetDrawScreen utf8rastport.library/URPDC_SetDrawScreen

    NAME
        URPDC_SetDrawScreen -- set the target screen, updating CLUT only if changed

    SYNOPSIS
        URPDC_SetDrawScreen(dc, screen)
                            A0  A1

        VOID URPDC_SetDrawScreen(struct URPDrawContext *dc,
                                 struct Screen *screen);

    FUNCTION
        Records screen as the current rendering target.  The internal
        RGB-to-CLUT remap table (and CLUT-mode glyph mirrors) are rebuilt
        only if the screen pointer differs from the previously recorded one.
        Use this for the common case of rendering onto the same screen every
        frame; it avoids unnecessary CLUT rebuilds on every draw call.

        When the screen has changed (e.g. the user switched screen modes),
        prefer URPDC_UpdateColorMap() which always rebuilds the remap table.

    INPUTS
        dc     -- target URPDrawContext.
        screen -- Intuition screen to associate with dc.

    RESULT
        None.

    SEE ALSO
        URPDC_UpdateColorMap

utf8rastport.library/URPDC_UpdateColorMap                                     \
                                    utf8rastport.library/URPDC_UpdateColorMap

    NAME
        URPDC_UpdateColorMap -- rebuild the RGB-to-CLUT remap table

    SYNOPSIS
        URPDC_UpdateColorMap(dc, screen)
                             A0  A1

        VOID URPDC_UpdateColorMap(struct URPDrawContext *dc,
                                  struct Screen *screen);

    FUNCTION
        Samples the colour map of screen's ViewPort and rebuilds the
        internal RGB-to-CLUT lookup table used to remap GRAY and RGBA
        glyph bitmaps onto indexed-colour (planar/chunky 8-bit) screens.
        Also flushes all CLUT-mode glyph mirrors so they are regenerated
        with the new palette on the next draw call.

        Call this once after the screen is opened, and again whenever the
        palette changes (e.g. after SetRGB32() / LoadRGB32()).

        Until this function has been called at least once, GRAY and RGBA
        glyphs are silently skipped when rendering onto an indexed screen.
        This does not affect MONO glyph rendering, which always works.

    INPUTS
        dc     -- target URPDrawContext.
        screen -- Intuition screen whose ViewPort.ColorMap is sampled.

    RESULT
        None.

    SEE ALSO
        URPDC_SetDrawScreen, URPDC_SetDrawColor, URPDrawTextUTF8
